1. What is Cilium?
Interview Question

What is Cilium and why do companies use it?

Answer

Cilium is a Kubernetes networking, security, and observability platform built on eBPF.

Traditional Kubernetes networking relies on:

iptables
kube-proxy
Linux networking rules

Cilium replaces much of this with eBPF programs running inside the Linux kernel.

Benefits:

Faster packet processing
Better scalability
Network policies
Observability
Load balancing
Service mesh without sidecars
2. What is eBPF?
Very Common
Answer

eBPF (Extended Berkeley Packet Filter) allows programs to run safely inside the Linux kernel.

Instead of packets traveling through many networking layers:

Plain Text
Packet
|
iptables
|
kube-proxy
|
routing
|
pod

Cilium attaches eBPF programs directly in the kernel.

Plain Text
Packet
|
eBPF
|
Pod

Result:

lower latency
fewer context switches
better performance
